  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "$-5+6=$",
  "worked_solution": "**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $6$ to $-5,$ we start at $-5$ on a number line and move $6$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14149949/assets/a33a6894112c333711ee25f2bb79abd458448d5c0d4131ddbc53f4f828cc161e.png)\n\nWe end up at $1.$ So, $-5+6=1.$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-5+6=6-5=1\n$$",
